# LugalOS Computer Algebra System (CAS) — Overview & Index

Documentation > User Manual > Computer Algebra System (CAS)

LugalOS features a self-contained, exact Computer Algebra System (CAS) written in Scheme-like Lisp. All computations use exact rational \mathbb{Q} and Gaussian rational \mathbb{Q}(i) arithmetic with zero floating-point overhead.

## 1. System Startup

From the LugalOS interactive shell (lsh), launch the Lisp REPL and load the CAS loader:

```lisp
lsh> lisp
lisp> (load "/sd0/cas/cas.lisp")
=> #t
```

Return to the shell at any time using (exit) or (quit).

## 2. Specialized Manuals & Modular Topics

The CAS documentation is partitioned into focused, lightweight manuals:

* algebra: Polynomials, equation solving (solve), canonical simplification (simplify, expand), partial fractions (apart), linear algebra (matrices), and infix calculator mode (calc).
* calculus: Symbolic differentiation (diff, derivative), integration (integrate, integrate-def), limits (limit), Taylor series (taylor), and trigonometric reductions (trig-expand, trig-reduce).
* plot: 2D Cartesian graphing, multi-curve plotting (plot-multi), parametric curves (plot-parametric), derivative comparison (plot-diff), and canvas graphics.

## 3. Quick Examples by Domain

### Algebra & Solving
```lisp
;; Canonical simplification and polynomial expansion
(simplify '(+ (* 3 x) (* 2 x) 5 -2))      ;; => (+ 3 (* 5 x))
(expand '(* (+ x 1) (+ x -1)))            ;; => (+ -1 (^ x 2))

;; Exact equation solving
(solve '(= (+ (^ x 2) (* -5 x) 6) 0) 'x)  ;; => (2 3)
```

### Calculus & Analysis
```lisp
;; Symbolic derivatives: d/dx [sin(2x)] = 2*cos(2x)
(diff '(sin (* 2 x)) 'x)                  ;; => (* 2 (cos (* 2 x)))

;; Indefinite integration: \int x * exp(x) dx
(integrate '(* x (exp x)) 'x)             ;; => (* (exp x) (+ -1 x))

;; 5th-order Taylor series of sin(x)
(taylor '(sin x) 'x 0 5)                  ;; => (+ x (* -1/6 (^ x 3)) (* 1/120 (^ x 5)))
```

### Visual Graphing
```lisp
(load "/sd0/cas/plot.lisp")
;; Plot curve and its derivative side-by-side
(plot-diff "x*sin(x)" '(x -6 6) '((title . "f(x) & f'(x)") (samples . 60)))

;; Plot multiple curves simultaneously
(plot-multi '("cos(x)" "1 - x^2/2") '(x -3 3) '((title . "Taylor vs Cos") (samples . 60)))
```

## 4. Master Function Index

```
| Category | Function | Signature | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Algebra | simplify | (simplify expr) | Canonical term reduction |
| Algebra | expand | (expand expr) | Distribute multiplications |
| Algebra | factor | (factor poly var) | Factor polynomial over Q |
| Algebra | solve | (solve eq var) | Exact equation solving |
| Algebra | apart | (apart expr var) | Partial fraction decomposition |
| Calculus | diff | (diff expr var [n]) | Symbolic differentiation |
| Calculus | integrate | (integrate expr var) | Indefinite integration |
| Calculus | integrate-def | (integrate-def e v a b) | Definite integration |
| Calculus | limit | (limit expr var x0) | Limit evaluation |
| Calculus | taylor | (taylor expr var x0 n) | Taylor series expansion |
| Plotting | plot | (plot "expr" '(x min max))| 2D function plotting |
| Plotting | plot-multi | (plot-multi '("f1" "f2") ...)| Multi-curve plotting |
| Plotting | plot-diff | (plot-diff "expr" ...) | Function vs derivative plot |
```

